# `core.autocrlf=true` is Git for Windows' default, so a fresh clone would
# otherwise arrive with CRLF endings while every generator here writes "\n".
# `npm test` compares committed files against regenerated text byte for byte
# (components/resume/resume.css against lib/render/metrics.ts), so that
# mismatch fails the suite on a clean checkout with a diff of two lines that
# look identical. Pinning the checkout to LF keeps disk and generator agreed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these, whatever they contain.
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.pdf   binary
